# CssUI Revival - Project TODO

## Pre-existing Issues
- [ ] Fix nullable reference warnings (many throughout codebase)

## Phase 8: Replace MetaEnum System with EnumRecords Package
Migrate from the runtime reflection-based MetaEnum system to EnumRecords' compile-time source generation. The `Lookup.Get_Keywords<T>()` usages are for populating keyword whitelists at static initialization — these can be replaced with a simple helper using `Enum.GetValues<T>()`.

### 8.1 Setup
- [x] Add EnumRecords NuGet package to CssUI.csproj — `dotnet add package EnumRecords`

### 8.2 Create Shared Property Record Structs
Create new file CssUI/Common/EnumProperties.cs:
- [x] `record struct KeywordProperties([ReverseLookup(IgnoreCase = true)] string Keyword)` — for ~60 keyword-only enums
- [x] `record struct UrlSchemeProperties([ReverseLookup(IgnoreCase = true)] string Keyword, int DefaultPort)` — for EUrlScheme
Note: ECssUnit can use KeywordProperties (keyword IS the unit symbol)

### 8.3 Migrate Enums
Replace `[MetaEnum]`/`[MetaKeyword]` with `[EnumRecord<T>]`/`[EnumData]`:
- [x] CSS/Enums/ (~40 enums)
- [x] DOM/Enums/ (~13 enums)
- [x] HTML/Enums/ (~22 enums)
- [x] URL/ (EUrlScheme)
- [x] CORE/Devices/ (EKeyboardCode, EPointerType)
- [x] Added NamedColorProperties for EColor (keyword + hex + RGB)

### 8.4 Update Lookup.cs Helper
Add helper method to preserve existing API signature for 40+ call sites:
- [x] Add `Get_Keywords<T>()` implementation using reflection to call generated Keyword() method
- [ ] Mark legacy EnumMetaTable-based methods as obsolete (defer to 8.5)

### 8.5 Update Consumer Call Sites
- [x] `Lookup.Get_Keyword(enumValue)` → `enumValue.Keyword()` (completed for direct usages)
- [x] `Lookup.TryGet_Enum<T>(keyword, out result)` → `TExtensions.TryFromKeyword(keyword, out result)` (completed for direct usages)

### 8.5.1 Migrate Remaining MetaEnum-based Enums to EnumRecords
These enums still use `[MetaEnum]`/`[MetaKeyword]` and need migration:
- [x] `EDisplayMode` (CSS/Enums/Style Properties/) - used by DisplayType.cs
- [x] `EBorderStyle` (CSS/Enums/Style Properties/) - border styling enum
- [x] `ECssValueTypes` (CSS/Enums/) - NO MIGRATION NEEDED: plain Flags enum, no keywords

### 8.5.2 Address Generic/Runtime Lookup Usages
These use `Lookup.TryKeyword<T>`/`Lookup.Keyword<T>` with generic type parameters.
**RESOLVED:** `Lookup.cs` already provides reflection-based bridge methods that call generated EnumRecords extensions.

- [x] `AtomicName<T>` (CORE/Types/Atomic/AtomicName.cs) - Uses Lookup.TryKeyword<T>, works via reflection bridge
- [x] `DOMEnumList<EnumType>` (DOM/Elements/Attributes/Base/DOMEnumList.cs) - Uses Lookup.Keyword<T>, works via reflection bridge
- [x] `AttributeValue.From<T>` (DOM/Elements/Attributes/AttributeValue.cs) - Uses Lookup.TryKeyword<T>, works via reflection bridge
- [x] `Serializer.Identifier<Ty>` (CSS/Serialization/Serializer.cs) - Uses Lookup.Keyword<T>, works via reflection bridge

### 8.5.3 Address Runtime Type Lookup Usages
These determine enum type at runtime and cannot use compile-time extension methods:
**RESOLVED:** `Lookup.Keyword(Type, object)` method provides runtime dispatch via reflection to EnumRecords extensions.

- [x] `CSSValue.ToString()` (CSS/Value/Base/CSSValue.cs) - Uses Lookup.Keyword(Type, object), works via reflection bridge

### 8.6 Cleanup
- [ ] Delete MetaEnumAttribute.cs (CORE/MetaTables/)
- [ ] Delete MetaKeywordAttribute.cs (CORE/MetaTables/)
- [ ] Delete EnumMetaTable.cs (CORE/MetaTables/)
- [ ] Delete EnumTables.cs (Common/)
- [ ] Remove obsolete methods in Lookup.cs
- [ ] Update LookupTests.cs to verify new extension methods

### 8.7 EnumRecords 0.4.1 Upgrade (Breaking Changes)
EnumRecords 0.4+ requires ALL enum members to have `[EnumData]` or `[Ignore]`.
v0.4.1 fixes char literal escaping in generated code.

#### 8.7.1 Fix Missing Attribute Errors (ENUMREC002)
Add `[Ignore]` to enum members without keywords:
- [x] `EKeyboardCode.MAX` (CORE/Devices/Keyboard/Enums/)
- [x] `EPointerType.MAX` (CORE/Devices/Pointer/Enums/)
- [x] `EMediaFeatureName.Unknown` (CSS/Enums/Media Properties/)
- [x] `EMediaQueryModifier.None` (CSS/Enums/Media Properties/)
- [x] `EMediaType.NONE` (CSS/Enums/Media Properties/)
- [x] `EScrollBehavior.Instant` (CSS/Enums/Style Properties/)
- [x] `ESelectorCombinator.None` (CSS/Enums/Style Properties/)
- [x] `ECssPropertyID.MAX_VALUE` (CSS/Properties/Enums/)
- [x] `EAttributeName.CUSTOM` (DOM/Enums/Attributes/Base/)
- [x] `EEventName.CUSTOM` (DOM/Events/Enums/)
- [x] `EContentEditable.Invalid`, `EContentEditable.Missing` (HTML/Enums/)
- [x] `EDraggable.Auto` (HTML/Enums/)

#### 8.7.2 Fix Argument Count Errors (ENUMREC003)
`EKeyboardCode` uses 2-arg attributes for `KeyboardCodeProperties(Keyword, KeyChar)`:
- [x] `KeyboardCodeProperties` already defined in EnumProperties.cs
- [x] Updated `[EnumRecord<KeywordProperties>]` to `[EnumRecord<KeyboardCodeProperties>]` on EKeyboardCode
- [x] Added second argument (KeyChar) to all single-argument EnumData entries (~60 entries)
- [x] Fixed `Lang1` which had 3 arguments (reduced to 2)

#### 8.7.3 Update Lookup.Get_Keywords() to Use New API
EnumRecords 0.4+ provides `GetKeywords()` method on generated extensions:
- [ ] Update `Lookup.Get_Keywords<T>()` to call `TExtensions.GetKeywords()` instead of reflection loop
- [ ] Handle enums that may not have GetKeywords() gracefully

